---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout activeTab="about" title="About | Viraj Sawad">
  <main class="max-w-[680px] w-full mx-auto px-6 mb-32 flex-1 mt-12">
    <!-- Hero Header -->
    <header class="mb-20">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mb-4 text-on-surface">Viraj Sawad</h1>
      <p class="text-on-surface-variant font-sans text-xs tracking-wide uppercase font-bold">Kathmandu · KEC · 3rd year CS</p>
    </header>

    <!-- Background Section -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-primary font-bold text-xs uppercase tracking-widest mb-6 border-b border-outline-variant/10 pb-2">Background</h2>
      <div class="prose-custom text-on-surface leading-relaxed space-y-4">
        <p>
          Hey, I'm Viraj Sawad, a third-year Computer Engineering student at Kantipur Engineering College, Tribhuvan University, Kathmandu, Nepal.
        </p>
        <p>
          I work at the intersection of LLMs, multi-agent systems, and vision-language models. I'm part of the Fusemachines AI Fellowship (AIF 2026) and the Leapfrog Student Partnership Program (LSPP 5th cohort).
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Curiosity Section -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-primary font-bold text-xs uppercase tracking-widest mb-6 border-b border-outline-variant/10 pb-2">The Curiosity</h2>
      <div class="prose-custom text-on-surface leading-relaxed">
        Somewhere beneath the engineering, I'm genuinely curious about something harder to pin down: whether language models can have something like thought. Not agents calling tools, not chain-of-thought prompting, but actual internal reasoning. I don't have answers yet. That's kind of the point.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Writing Philosophy Section -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-primary font-bold text-xs uppercase tracking-widest mb-6 border-b border-outline-variant/10 pb-2">Writing Philosophy</h2>
      <div class="prose-custom text-on-surface leading-relaxed">
        I write about what I build, what I break, and what I'm still figuring out. Writing helps me think, so most posts here are honest, technical, and probably still half-wrong when I publish them.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Outside Work Section -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-primary font-bold text-xs uppercase tracking-widest mb-6 border-b border-outline-variant/10 pb-2">Outside work</h2>
      <div class="prose-custom text-on-surface leading-relaxed">
        When I am not writing code, I try to step away from the keyboard and engage with the physical world. You can usually find me going on runs, reading essays, or cooking and experimenting with new recipes. I also enjoy listening to music, trying new things, and journaling to clear my head and organize my thoughts.
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Find Me / Social Section -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-primary font-bold text-xs uppercase tracking-widest mb-8 border-b border-outline-variant/10 pb-2">Find me</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-6 font-sans text-sm">
        <a href="https://github.com/VirajSawad1021" target="_blank" class="text-on-surface font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-primary transition-colors duration-200">GitHub</a>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/viraj-sawad-92970a33b/" target="_blank" class="text-on-surface font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-primary transition-colors duration-200">LinkedIn</a>
        <a href="https://www.instagram.com/viraj_sawad/" target="_blank" class="text-on-surface font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-primary transition-colors duration-200">Instagram</a>
        <a href="mailto:virajsawad07@gmail.com" class="text-on-surface font-semibold underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-primary transition-colors duration-200">Email</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
